            <ArticleTitle>Osteoid osteoma of the proximal phalanx of a toe. A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>102-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of osteoid osteoma of proximal phalanx of second toe is presented. The clinical, radiological, and pathological features are discussed. Osteoid osteoma is rare in toe phalanges but should be considered when a patient presents with unexplained chronic pain in his or her toes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
